    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284-a7">

                <pb facs="0542" n="532" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg532"/>

                <opener>[Enclosure 7 in No. 21.]</opener>
                <head>Viscount Monck to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Government House,
                            Quebec</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your excellency’s despatch of the 13th, enclosing copy of a note from
                    the Secretary of State of the United States, demanding the extradition of John
                    C. Braine, H. A. Parr, John Parker Locke, <hi rendition="#italic">alias</hi>
                    Vernon G. Locke, David Collins, George Robinson, and John Wade, fugitives from
                    the justice of the United States.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform your excellency that I have referred this
                    application to the law officers of the crown in Canada for their report.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <p rendition="#right">MONCK.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
